Z||000003||TROX||05-31-2001||08:34 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by baptistheart:<BR><B>Correct me if i'm wrong but i thought i seen a conversion kit for $35 at auto zone says it will convert any car it's just different fittings for the setup you have now.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>This is just a charge, you muse clean out the system and then figure out how much 134a you will need (Its less than the R22 in you system) This is if the compressor is good and no other problems.<BR>ed <P>------------------<BR>||||reg||14
Z||000004||TROX||05-31-2001||08:35 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by baptistheart:<BR><B>Correct me if i'm wrong but i thought i seen a conversion kit for $35 at auto zone says it will convert any car it's just different fittings for the setup you have now.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>This is just a charge, you must clean out the system and then figure out how much 134a you will need (Its less than the R22 in you system) This is if the compressor is good and no other problems.<BR>ed <P>------------------<BR>||||reg||14
Z||000005||Fformula88||05-31-2001||09:10 PM||||My compressor leaks the stuff out of it, so I decided to give the $35 134 kit a shot.  The kit comes with a few cans of the stuff and a can of oil/lubricant for the compressor.  I figured I could get thru the summer with it.<P>The stuff works fine in the system.  It gets very cold and the charge lasted the whole summer.  Over the course of the winter it will all leak out and not work in the spring again, but a couple more cans gets it working great!<P>The reason that it should be professionally emptied of R12 is to prevent it from escaping into the atmosphere.  Also, the new gas will leak thru some older types of rubber hoses depending on their chemical makeup.  I do not know if the Fiero uses these types of lines or not.<P>A $1800 quote is a rip-off since there is nothing fancy to these conversions.  They are probably selling new evaporators, condensors and such because people think they need to be "converted".  If the compressor is shot, it isn't gonna work and you will need a new one.  Otherwise, just try the $35 kit.||||reg||1
Z||000006||hugh||05-31-2001||09:37 PM||||First freon 22 has never been used in an automotive application that I am aware of.Freon 12 was always used till it's production was cut back then stopped.134a became it's replacement even though it is about 10% less efficient than f12.I haven't done any automotive air,but I have talked to people that have and 134a works just fine.You need a set of gauges and access to a vacuum pump.Pep Boys sells a kit with oil and 134a and it works.You must be careful when working on the system,because the discharge pressure can reach 300 psi with prolonged idling.The ideal way is to replace the accumulator tank,o rings,and other suggested things,but it is NOT necessary.If your system is not empty then it has no contaminants because the pressure switch will not let it run in a vacuum and draw anything into the system.When freon leaks it usually carries oil with it,If you see any oil or greasy fittings determine if you have any pressure in the system,mix some soapy water(dish detergent is fine)and put it anywhere you suspect a leak.Fix,or get fixed any you find,put it on a vacuum pump add the oil,134a and enjoy the cool.If the compressor seal is leaking,again you will see a greasy area around the seal.It is cheaper to just charge the system than it is to replace the compressor as long as it isn't pouring out.I know this is a long post,but I can't let people believe that air conditioning is rocket science,it isn't!Just be careful.||||reg||1
Z||000007||MoneypitGT||05-31-2001||10:44 PM||||I picked up the kit from wal-mart, screwed on the fittings and charged it up. Works great, been a little over a year. Chris<P>------------------<BR><B>Check out my site at:</B>   <A HREF="http://www.customdynamix.com" TARGET=_blank>www.customdynamix.com</A> <BR>2 '87 GT Projects||||reg||14
